    description: "WHAT.\n1. The F# analyzer sets is_exported on no symbol and has no entrypoint pattern, so dead-code seeds are only the connectivity fallback: every public member nothing in the repository calls is a candidate.\n2. A call through an interface-typed value resolves to the abstract slot; there is no edge from slot to implementation (needs base_classes plus fsharp in the inheritance linker's depends_on).\n3. Base defect: `module M\\nlet f x = g x` with no final newline emits no f (the grammar rejects the last declaration). The one F# class in a cloned repository (vscode's colorize test) is lost this way.\n4. Base defect: nested `module A =` emits no module symbol, so the containment linker's naming phase binds A.run to a same-named type in another file.\n5. Not symbols: object-expression members, class-level let values, enum/delegate/exception/abbreviation types, the primary constructor; .fsi signature files do not parse.\n\nOnly two genuine F# files are cloned on the build machine. Found during PR 1 of the stable-id plan, 2026-11-15 (PR #2198). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr1/STATUS.md."  # bc7b
    fields: {}  # bc7b
